  "backbone_method": "Separate optimal rigid alignments for CA and N/CA/C/O, matching chain/residue number/atom name; all 160 residues. No ligand, side chains, sequence design, refolding or outlier trimming.",
  "limitations": [
    "One input/seed and two launches per setting; not a guarantee across GPUs, software versions, checkpoints, backends, shapes, or compiler-cache changes.",
    "One warm timing per setting; includes preprocessing, inference and structure writing. Startup timings include weight loading/compilation and are not warm speed measurements.",
    "Seed-controlled randomness and numerical reproducibility are distinct. Deterministic execution does not make different kernel implementations numerically equivalent.",
    "Initial tensors from the original four-pair pilot were not retained, so these controls do not establish the sole cause of its original replay discrepancy."
  ],
  "seed_identity_notes": [
    "Noise uses SHA256-derived seeds keyed by global seed, example ID, diffusion sample index and event tag, using true lengths before padding.",
    "Foundry example IDs may include the JSON filename or global_prefix and batch index. Preserve these when comparing runs.",
    "Pipelines adds chunk_id to seed_offset and uses chunk-dependent prefixes. Preserve chunk assignments for replay.",
    "The current Pipelines seed_offset=0 branch omits the seed override. This separate edge case did not affect these explicit seed-42 tests."
  ],
